Q1. What is Flutter? 

Flutter is an open-source UI toolkit by Google used to build cross-platform apps (Android, iOS, Web, Desktop) from a single codebase using Dart. 

  

Q2. What is Dart? 

Dart is a programming language developed by Google used to create Flutter apps. It is fast and optimized for UI development. 

   

Q3. What is a widget in Flutter? 

A widget is the basic building block of Flutter UI. Everything in Flutter is a widget. 

  

Q4. Types of widgets in Flutter? 

1. Stateless Widget - A widget whose UI does not change after it is created. 

2. Stateful Widget - A widget whose UI can change dynamically when data changes. 

 

Q5. Common widgets used in Flutter?  

* Text 

* Container 

* Row 

* Column 

* Image 

* Button 

* Scaffold 

* AppBar  

Q6. What is manifest.json? 

It is a JSON file that contains details of a Progressive Web App (PWA). 

 manifest.json contain : 

* App name 

* Icons 

* Theme color 

* Background color 

* Start URL 

* Display mode 
 
--> Why is manifest.json important? 

It makes the web app installable and improves user experience. 

 

Q7. What is Add to Home Screen? 

A feature that allows users to install a web app on mobile home screen like a native app. 

