Q1. What is PWA? 

Progressive Web App is a web application that works like a mobile app and can be installed on devices.  

--> advantages of PWA? 

Offline support, fast loading, installable, responsive design. 

 

  

Q2. What is GitHub Pages? 

GitHub Pages is a free hosting service by GitHub used to deploy static websites. 

  

Q3. Why use GitHub Pages for deployment? 

It is free, easy to use, and good for hosting frontend projects. 

  

Q4. What is the use of gh-pages package? 

It is used to publish React build files to GitHub Pages. 

  

Q5. What is the purpose of npm run build? 

It creates an optimized production version of the React app. 

  

Q6. What is the use of npm run deploy? 

It builds the project and uploads it to GitHub Pages. 

  

Q7. What is homepage in package.json? 

It defines the website URL where the app will be hosted. 

  

Q8. What is Git? 

Git is a version control system used to track code changes. 

  

Q9. What is GitHub? 

GitHub is an online platform used to store and manage Git repositories. 

  

Q10. What is repository? 

A repository is a storage space for project files and code. 

  

Q11. What is the use of git init? 

It initializes a new Git repository in the project folder. 

  

Q12. What is git add . command? 

It adds all files to staging area. 

  

Q13. What is git commit? 

It saves changes with a message in Git. 

  

Q14. What is git push? 

It uploads local project files to GitHub repository. 

  

Q15. What is branch in Git? 

A branch is a separate line of development in Git. 

  

Q16. What is main branch? 

It is the default primary branch of a repository. 

  

Q17. Why is React app suitable for GitHub Pages? 

Because React generates static files after build. 

  

Q18. Can backend be hosted on GitHub Pages? 

No, GitHub Pages supports only static frontend files. 

   

